{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode a deterministic exploration policy in small specifications. The policy favors random_walk in clear/search conditions, inserts a short move_forward pulse after a clear exploratory pulse for coverage, and routes every obstacle observation through a dedicated turn-recovery state. Action states self-loop on path_clear so intended one-shot controllable pulses are not preempted, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion with simple plant automata",
    "Use deterministic specification states with exactly one controllable action in each explore/recovery state",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward random_walk and short forward progress alternation",
    "Send obstacle_front to a dedicated front-recovery turn state, obstacle_left to clockwise recovery, and obstacle_right to counterclockwise recovery",
    "Return to exploration immediately on path_clear after recovery and avoid full_rotate except as an optional last-resort extension not needed here"
  ],
